  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till Nationell Statistik</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to National Statistics - Liberia National Statistics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ambassaden i Liberia fick en f&#xf6;rfr&#xe5;gan av FN&apos;s Befolkningsfond att financiera projektet &quot;National Population and Housing Census&quot; i Liberia med 70 miljoner SEK under perioden december 2018 till december 2022.

Huvudsyftet med st&#xf6;det &#xe4;r att genomf&#xf6;ra befolknings- och bostadsr&#xe4;kningen i Liberia f&#xf6;r att s&#xe5;ledes bidra till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra m&#xe4;nniskors livskvalitet genom att ge regeringen och relevanta akt&#xf6;rer uppdaterad och tillf&#xf6;rlitlig data om bland annat den sociala, demografiska och ekonomiska dimensionen hos Liberias befolkning. Detta omfattar definitionen av strategier f&#xf6;r fattigdomsbek&#xe4;mpning samt utarbetande av sociala och ekonomiska utvecklingsprogram p&#xe5; grundval av uppdaterad statistik och data.

Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r &quot;National Population and Housing Census&quot; projektet &#xe4;r 19 miljoner USD, varav v&#xe4;rdlandets egna finansiering uppg&#xe5;r till cirka 6.76 miljoner USD.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Liberia Embassy received a request from the United Nations Population Fund to finance the National Population and Housing Census project in Liberia with 70 million SEK during the period December 2018 to December 2022.

The main purpose of the contribution is to support the implemention of the National Population and Housing Census in Liberia, thus contributing to improving people&apos;s quality of life by providing updated and reliable data to the government and relevant actors, including the social, demographic and economic dimension of Liberia&apos;s population. This includes the definition of poverty reduction strategies and the preparation of social and economic development programs on the basis of updated statistics and data.

The total budget of the National Population and Housing Census project is 19 million USD, of which the host country&apos;s own funding amounts to approximately 6.76 million USD.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact: Government effectiveness is increased through evidence-based policy making, development, economic and governance planning, monitoring and evaluation.
Outcome: Validated accurate Census statistics that can be used with confidence for planning development outcomes.&#xa0;
Development objective:
Contribute to the improvement of quality of life of the people by providing the Government and other stakeholders with relevant, reliable, sufficient and timely social, demographic and economic data and information for development planning, policy formulation and service delivery as well as for monitoring and evaluation of development programmes and plans.</narrative>
  </description>
